    "# Conclusion\n",
    "\n",
    "## Validation\n",
    "This comparative analysis validates that the simultaneous orthogonal collocation framework accurately captures stiff continuous-time system dynamics. The close agreement between sequential and simultaneous methods confirms that the discrete-time CasADi formulation enables controllers to safely and reliably enforce probabilistic bounds under strict stochastic uncertainty.\n",
    "\n",
    "## Control\n",
    "The implementation of dynamic, piecewise control strategies proves significantly superior to static baseline approaches. By aggressively exploiting the early temporal degrees of freedom and subsequently throttling the feed and jacket temperatures ($T_0$ and $T_j$), the dynamic controller effectively \"surfs\" the 350 K safety boundary. This prevents the compounding variance cone from violating the 95% confidence limits, overcoming the paralyzing conservatism of constant control.\n",
    "\n",
    "## Physics & Performance\n",
    "From a physical standpoint, the ability to operate dynamically near the thermal constraint boundary directly serves the primary objective of maximizing the integral of $c_A$. By safely jump-starting the reaction kinetics and fully utilizing the reactor's admissible thermal capacity, the dynamic optimization strategies unlock a higher cumulative product yield while successfully mitigating the risks of thermal runaway posed by kinetic and thermodynamic variations."
